{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Maria:</strong> Hi, Steve, were you in the software programming class?</p>\n<p><strong>Steven:</strong> Hi! No, I wasn&rsquo;t there, I was in the library. I was reading about human-readable medium in computing.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Maria: </strong>I almost forgot! We have to write an essay about human-readable medium.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Steven:</strong> Yes, I want to do it step by step as the teacher told us. You know: <i>&ldquo;read about the topic and take notes of the most relevant ideas, don&rsquo;t copy literary from the source, support your ideas&rdquo;. </i></p>\n<p><strong>Maria</strong>: Yes, it&rsquo;s better to stick to the teacher&rsquo;s instructions. What was the title of the book you read?</p>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Steven</strong>: It was a great book! It is called <i>&ldquo;Human-Readable Media, the Next Frontier&rdquo;. </i>The author explains that human-readable media is a term we use not only to refer to all the data and information humans are able to understand, but also refers to short data strings that are easy to remember. I wrote some sentences about the topic, look!</p>\n<p><strong>Maria</strong>: <i>&ldquo;Programmers encode human-readable medium in languages such as ASCII and Unicode, which are far from the computers&rsquo; binary representation of data</i>&rdquo;. I don&rsquo;t understand why we cannot codify all the information into human-readable representations.</p>", "time": "41000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob06re2img03.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Steven</strong>: There wasn&rsquo;t enough information in the library about codification, but I know that programmers prefer binary formats because they take less space for storage; in addition to that, binary codes are the language of computers, so programs run faster when they don&rsquo;t need to translate text into binary representations.</p>\n<p><strong>Maria</strong>: So, what can we humans do to understand encrypted information?</p>\n<p><strong>Steven</strong>: There are some useful devices we have to use to translate the codes into human readable information; for example, those machines to read the barcodes show us human-readable information hidden in the bars. There are also product tags with both human and machine readable data.</p>", "time": "86000"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 3, "type": "video", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "enpe7n2le01ob06re5vsc01", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "", "text": "", "time": "0"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can read about human-readable medium.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write sentences correctly to express my understanding about the topic.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can exchange information about human-readable medium with correct and precise sentences.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How do you think people can read codes in programming? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you need to read codes? Explain?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"c